     Colour tokens on body, not on .doc: the sticky bar lives outside .doc, and with the tokens on
     .doc its button came out transparent with white text on white, which is invisible.

     The selector is `html body`, not plain `body`, on purpose. In production the layout's inline
     style comes AFTER this file, both weigh the same, and the later one won: the page shipped dark
     although it was light on a laptop. The extra `html` raises the weight and removes the
     dependency on load order. Only a live request catches this; the build says nothing. */
  html body { background: #F5F2EC; color: #0B1017;
         --card: #fff; --line: rgba(11,16,23,.09); --ink-2: #4A5362; --muted: #6B7480;
